# Real Firebase config is environment-specific and contains project keys.
# Copy app/google-services.json.example to app/google-services.json and fill it in.
app/google-services.json

# Release signing keys hold the app's upload/signing identity, never committed. CI decodes the
# keystore from the SIGNING_STORE_BASE64 secret into the workspace at build time, which is why this
# has to cover the whole tree rather than one directory.
*.jks
*.keystore

# A Firebase service-account private key can send push to every installed user and read the whole
# project. Keep it outside the repository entirely; this is only a backstop against a stray copy.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
service-account*.json

# Working notes for whoever is shipping (console steps, release checklist, idea backlog). Untracked
# deliberately: it is a scratchpad, not documentation, and it changes every session. Start one by
# copying ACTIONS.template.md.
ACTIONS.md

# Smoke-test output (screenshots, logcat captures, reports). Evidence of one run on one device.
smoke_logcat.txt

# A crashed JVM (the Gradle daemon included) writes these to the working directory root, not to
# build/. hs_err_pid10106.log/replay_pid10106.log slipped into a commit once already.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log